Ensure safe custody of Commission records and accountable documents;
Validate monthly bank reconciliations statements;
Confirm the accuracy and completeness of accounts receivables (invoicing, receipting, banking and reconciliations) and reporting on the same as appropriate;
Process payroll and reconciliation;
Ensure that statutory deductions are accurate and remitted on time;
Maintain staff imprest and advances ledgers;
Assist in preparing financial management reports; and
Any other duties that might be assigned to the Officer from time to time.
Qualifications
For appointment to this grade, a candidate must have:
A Bachelor’s degree in Commerce (Accounting option); Commerce (Finance option); Business Administration (Accounting option) or equivalent qualification from a recognized institution;
Master’s degree is an added advantage;
Certified Public Accountants Kenya (CPA) / ACCA Finalist;
Be a member in good standing of a professional body;
Supervisory course lasting not less than two (2) weeks;
At least four (4) years of experience;
Proficiency in the usage of recognized computer accounting software and common office applications;
Demonstrate competence in work performance and results; and
Fulfil the requirements of Chapter Six of the Constitution.
Terms Of Service And Remuneration
The appointment will be on permanent terms of employment. An attractive remunerative package, commensurate to qualifications, experience and responsibilities and in line with Government guidelines will be offered to the successful applicant.
